    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:Philip has 20 cows. Philip has 50% more ducks, which means he has 50/100 * 20 = 10 more ducks. So Philip has a total of 20 + 10 = 30 cows and ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. One-fifth of ducks and cows in total is 1/5 * (30 + 10) = 1/5 * 40 = 8. So Philip has 8 pigs. In total, Philip has 30 cows + 10 ducks + 8 pigs = 48 cows + 10 ducks + 8 pigs = 56 cows + 10 ducks + 8 pigs = 76 animals on his farm. #### 76 The answer is: 76

